Your rules for this feature, as the builders will follow them (each one applies to every case like it, not just the example):
  1. Whenever a refund window is counted, count the days from the delivery date, not from the order date.
  2. Whenever a refund is requested, the owner's policy decides and pays it automatically, with no approval step. No request is held for approval because of its amount, so ₹15,000 and ₹900 are treated alike.
  3. Whenever an order is final-sale and its goods did not arrive damaged, no refund is given. Damage is the only exception, and no other condition or special case (such as opened goods, gift cards or custom orders) restricts refunds.
  4. Whenever goods arrived damaged (including final-sale goods) and the request is made up to 90 days after delivery, the full refund is paid, including the shipping fee. Whenever a request for damaged goods is made more than 90 days after delivery, nothing is paid.
  5. Whenever an order is returned, the base refund amount is the price of the returned items minus any discount code applied (for example ₹5,000 − ₹1,000 = ₹4,000 for Meena's coat). The discount-code amount is not refunded.
  6. Whenever goods are not damaged, the shipping fee paid on the order is not refunded (for example, Arjun's jacket is refunded ₹3,000 and none of the ₹200 shipping fee). No rule about return shipping is applied.
  7. Whenever a refund is paid, it goes back to the payment method(s) the order was originally paid with, regardless of what the customer asks for. Card orders are refunded to the card (so Ravi's ₹6,000 lamp return goes to his card, not store credit), and store-credit orders are refunded as store credit. There is no special rule for loyalty points.
  8. Whenever a refund for goods that are not damaged comes to less than 100 rupees, it is not paid. Refunds for damaged goods are paid whatever the amount.
  9. Whenever an order is placed and paid for, the customer earns one loyalty point for every full ₹50 paid for the items after the discount code is applied (so a ₹1,000 order earns 20 points). Shipping and tax are not counted. There are no category bonuses and no special treatment of sale items.
  10. Whenever an order is a final-sale order, it earns double points (so a ₹1,000 final-sale order earns 40 points).
  11. Whenever an order is paid with store credit, it earns no points.
  12. Whenever the items on an order come to less than ₹500 after the discount code is applied, the order earns no points.
  13. Whenever an order is returned, even for a full refund, the points earned on that order are not taken back.
  14. Whenever points have been earned, they never expire, so points earned at any time, including two years ago, stay available.
  15. Priya asks for a refund 34 days after delivery for goods that are not damaged. Is she refunded, or is she paid nothing because it is after day 30? -> B. For goods that are not damaged, within 7 days of delivery is full, day 8 to day 30 is half, and after day 30 nothing, so Priya at day 34 gets nothing.
  16. Can customers spend their loyalty points? -> B. No, customers only earn points and never spend them, and there is no rule for paying with points.
